A||||7||fieroX||a story about my wreck, a dumb old man and his insurance company.||||1||
Z||000000||fieroX||11-17-2001||04:44 AM||||I made a post last week about an accident I was in, where an old guy pulled into the side of my car while changing lanes.  At first he made it out to be my fault, but as I analyzed the scenerio over and over in my head I finally realized he was at fault.  Oh well, I said.  I was going to let it go.  I came out of the wreck with a popped tire, a scuffed up rim, a few scuffs on my paint and a misaligned window that is very hard to roll up and down.  So the other day I get a call from my insurance guy saying I had a guy trying to make a claim against me.  I was pissed.  The officer said no one was at fault.  which I think was bs.  My insurance guy took my recorded statement, and immediately told me he was at fault, and to contact his insurance and file a claim.  so I did.  Later that night I called the guy I got in the wreck with and asked him why he filed against my insurance, at first he acted like he didnt know what was going on, and denyed it.  but I was like "my insurance company contacted me and told me you did"  then he admitted to it.  so he told me he was advised by his insurance guy to file the claim, but earlier that evening when I filed against him, his insurance guy didnt know a thing about it.  so he told me that he felt it was my fault and he filed against me, had it estimated, and my insurance was cutting the check for the repairs.  Well my insurance guy told me different, he said he had written a real nice letter of denial that is in plain english that anyone could understand, and it was going to be mailed the next day.  So I asked the guy if I could come over to his house and take some pictures of the damage.  He said ok.  so I lined my car up exactly with his at the point of impact and began shooting pics.  my evidence against him is overwhelming.  My car is exactly beside his at the point of impact, and he trys to tell the cops that I went around him and swerved back to hit him, Im like "then how would I get forced into the curb if I hit him?"  <BR>So the next day his insurance gets back with me after reviewing all the evidence and both recorded statements, and theyre going to pay me.  I take my car in tuesday to get it estimated, and im taking the cash money straight to the bank.  Im paying off my car loan, and one of my 3 credit cards.  I can deal with a messed up door until next spring.  BTW, I had the damages estimated by a local body shop, and to fix the paint damage on the driver side only (I didnt discover the damage on the pass side until tonight) and to fix the window and door hinge, it was $923.02.  So + the popped tire and messed up rim + another alignment + the messed up paint on the front fascia....$$$$ hell yeah.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||11-17-2001||08:15 AM||||I had a funny case while I lived in NJ.  I pulled into my driveway and stopped my car to get my mail.  I reached down to open my door and I feel the earth move.  Lady came across my front yard and hit the pass side of my Astre Lil Wide Track.  Long story short I had to go to court because she had so many accidents that the insurance co. was going to drop her if she lost this one.  Her lawer thied to say I was my fault because I passed her at a traffic lite four miles before my driveway. Said if I hadn't passed her the accident wouldn't have happened.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||11-17-2001||08:22 AM||||Man, that sounds almost exactly like what happened to my wife last year when her car was 1 week old.  She was making a right turn into our driveway with signal on, when some old guy in a lincoln town car tries to pass her on the right against the curb and scrapes down her right side.  The first I hear about it is the guy and his wife screaming at my wife in front ouf our house. The damage didn't look too bad, just scraped paint and plastic, no bent metal so I just told them to take it easy and we would each file our own ins.  The guy's wife starts yelling, "OH NO!! You're paying for this, I've already called the cops on my cell phone!"  We were much luckier than you in that the cop was pretty sharp and wrote up the report assigning 100% fault to the guy in the Lincoln.  He lied and told his ins. co. that it was our fault so I got a call from them a few days later asking for $$.  I just faxed them the copy of the police report that I had gotten from the municipal offices and the ins guy got really pissed at his driver for lying to him.  We took the car to one of the best body shops in town and they charged their ins $980 for a scraped fender.  I could have gotten it fixed at another shop for Probably &lt;$300.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||11-17-2001||01:35 PM||||Good for you!  Most of us out here aren't greedy, but when people do sh*t like that, you can't help it.  I was in an accident on August 23rd.  I was backing out of my spot, and some *******  came through the lot at about 35 and took the back end off.  And he gave me a BS story.  Then he left.  So the cops called him, and he said that he did that because he had no license for 10 years.  You'd think that would be enough for me to collect.  Wrong.  We went after his insurance company, and they denied it, saying that the stories contradicted each other; nevermind that they never even called to ask me what happened.  Then a few weeks later, we got mail from his insurance company asking us for $2600.  Then we decided to take the dick to court.  There he gave a horse-sh*t story, lied about everything, and we eventually won.  I get my $2800 by December 5th.  Don't let him intimidate you.  Take your $1000+ and enjoy it.   ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||11-17-2001||03:22 PM||||Up here in Canada, we can't just pocket the money. Helps out in fraud schemes. We get an estimate voucher, which the mechanic fills out, then the repairs are made. Sign the form, and pay the deductible there and then, unless there's no fault. <BR>While I agree that the other bugger was at fault, I'm not so happy that you didn't get the car fixed... That's what the insurance is THERE for, isn't it? Whatever, there's nothing inherently WRONG with it...||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||11-17-2001||04:09 PM||||I see nothing wrong with not fixing the car and just pocketing the money. All he is doing is collecting for damages. If he decides not to fix the car, there is still that damage. <P>I liken it to someone causing $1000 damage to a $400 car. Scrap the car, get $100 from the yard, and your up $700 from where you were. Sounds like a plan if it ever happens to me.||||reg||1
Z||000006||TylerB11||11-17-2001||04:29 PM||||My older brother pulled that one off...<P>He had an 85 Celica GTS convertible. (Nice car) so he hits a guard rail on rte 80 in a rainstorm, ruining the front end. Well it seems that the previous owner had messed the car up pretty good before that. Anyways he buys a Celica GTS hatchback to get the front end for $1200. It had an oil leak, which he fixed and drove until he switched the parts (it was a different color and would have needed painting) well to make a short story long, some asswipe hit his rear quarter panel, and his insurance paid $1700. So he got the front end of the car, and made 500 bucks on the deal. Not bad.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Borgio||11-17-2001||07:20 PM||||Something like that happened to me. But they are paying you for the amount of damages, enough to get your car like it was, and they should. It liquidates your "investment", but that's all. They could care less what you do with the money. Now fraud that's different, and i can see how vauchers could help with that. But it doesn't benefit anyone except the repair place to fix it if you don't want it fixed. And the repair shop certainly isn't entitled to anything. To take the money and deposit it isn't unethical or immoral. It's just like a court settlement, you don't have to spend the money you get on the same thing you lost. Fixing something more than you care about getting it fixed is just a waste, but you did lose something by their doing and they should pay for it.||||reg||1
